@page "/triage-demo"

@* The triage demo (F106.3.4): one real error of the made-up order service, triaged by the team and recorded once,
   played back step by step with the agent at work lit and a popup per step, then the offer. A live run takes its
   place when the workflow lands (F106.3.3). The Demos menu and the demo index lead here (F122). Two columns (F122):
   the words, the team and the controls on the left, the step and the run so far on the right. *@

<PageTitle>Watch a triage · louis-agent</PageTitle>
<PageDescription Text="Watch a team of louis-agent agents triage a real error: sort it, find the cause, fix it on a branch with a test and review the fix." />

<Band Id="top" Kicker="The triage team" Paged="false">
    <TriagePlayer Source="recordings/triage-run.jsonl">
        <Intro>
            <h2 class="chrome">Watch a team triage a real error.</h2>
            <p class="lede">A made-up order service failed on a retired discount code. A team of agents sorts the error, decides what it gets, finds the cause, fixes it on a branch with a test, and reviews the fix, while code between them checks every step. This is that run, recorded once and played back. Nothing runs while you watch.</p>
        </Intro>
        <Actions>
            <GuideButton Class="is-plain" Question="I watched the triage team fix the order service. What just happened, and could I get a team like that?">Ask the guide what happened</GuideButton>
        </Actions>
        <Ending>
            <p class="recorded-offer">Want a team like this on your own services? <a href="/contact">Ask for yours</a>.</p>
        </Ending>
    </TriagePlayer>
</Band>
